---
import Layout from '../components/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | GoZeroShot"
  description="Privacy Policy for GoZeroShot's social-media distribution, publishing, analytics, and marketing-automation tools, including what data is received via platform authorization and how deletion requests are handled."
>
  <main class="main legal-page">
    <section class="legal-shell">
      <a class="back-link" href="/">Back to home</a>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="effective-date">Last updated: September 21, 2026</p>

      <p>
        GoZeroShot ("GoZeroShot," "we," or "us") builds internal and
        potentially client-facing tools for social-media distribution,
        publishing, analytics, and marketing automation. This Privacy Policy
        explains what information we may receive, how we use it, and how you
        can request deletion. Questions or requests can be sent to
        <a href="mailto:alynch@gozeroshot.dev">alynch@gozeroshot.dev</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Platforms we may connect to</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on the workflow, GoZeroShot may connect to authorized
        accounts on platforms such as Pinterest, TikTok, X, LinkedIn,
        Meta/Facebook/Instagram, YouTube, Bluesky, Buffer, Medium, Hashnode,
        Google Ads, Mixpanel, and Google Analytics (GA4). This list describes
        possible integrations only. GoZeroShot does not claim partnership,
        certification, endorsement, or approved-access status from any
        platform, and not every integration is active for every user or
        client.
      </p>

      <h2>Information we may receive</h2>
      <p>
        After you explicitly connect an account through a platform's OAuth
        or authorization flow, and only within the scopes you grant, we may
        receive:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>account and profile identifiers</li>
        <li>the authorization scopes you granted</li>
        <li>connected Pages, Boards, channels, or business accounts</li>
        <li>content and media you select to submit through the tool</li>
        <li>publishing status and platform object IDs (e.g. post or campaign IDs) returned after an action</li>
        <li>performance, analytics, and advertising data made available by the platform</li>
        <li>technical logs needed for security, debugging, and troubleshooting</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How we use this information</h2>
      <p>We use the information above to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>connect and maintain authorized platform accounts</li>
        <li>create drafts of user-approved content</li>
        <li>schedule and publish content you have approved</li>
        <li>retrieve reporting, analytics, and performance data</li>
        <li>test sandbox or non-delivering advertising integrations</li>
        <li>operate the specific automation workflow you requested</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>We do not sell personal information</h2>
      <p>
        GoZeroShot does not sell personal information. We do not use platform
        data received under this policy for unrelated advertising or resale
        purposes.
      </p>

      <h2>Sharing of information</h2>
      <p>
        We share information only where necessary to operate the requested
        workflow: with the connected platform itself (to publish, read, or
        report on your behalf), with infrastructure or hosting providers that
        run the tool, or where required by law. We do not share connected
        account data with unrelated third parties.
      </p>

      <h2>Data retention</h2>
      <p>
        We retain connected-account information for as long as the
        integration remains active and for as long as needed to operate the
        requested workflow, maintain basic operational records, resolve
        disputes, or comply with legal obligations. When you revoke access or
        request deletion, we remove the data we hold as described below.
      </p>

      <h2>Revoking access and requesting deletion</h2>
      <p>
        You can revoke GoZeroShot's access to a connected platform account at
        any time from that platform's own app/connection settings (for
        example, the platform's "Apps" or "Connected Accounts" page). You can
        also request deletion of the data GoZeroShot holds by emailing
        <a href="mailto:alynch@gozeroshot.dev">alynch@gozeroshot.dev</a>. See
        the <a href="/data-deletion">Data Deletion</a> page for details on
        what to include in that request.
      </p>
      <p>
        Deleting data stored by GoZeroShot does not automatically delete
        content that has already been published to an external platform.
        Removing published content requires action on that platform directly.
      </p>

      <h2>What we do not do</h2>
      <p>
        We do not ask you to submit passwords, tokens, secrets, cookies,
        recovery codes, or OAuth authorization codes through chat, email, or
        any public form. Account connections happen only through each
        platform's own official authorization flow.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        We take reasonable steps to protect the information described in this
        policy, but no system can guarantee absolute security. We do not
        claim specific encryption standards, certifications, or compliance
        programs unless stated elsewhere in writing.
      </p>

      <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>
        GoZeroShot is not intended for children under 13, and we do not
        knowingly collect personal information from children.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Continued use of
        the site or related tools after an update means the revised policy
        applies.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Privacy questions or deletion requests can be sent to
        <a href="mailto:alynch@gozeroshot.dev">alynch@gozeroshot.dev</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    display: block;
  }

  .legal-shell {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
    border-radius: 18px;
    padding: 2rem;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: #4a6f98;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 2.2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  h2 {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }

  p {
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
  }

  ul {
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 0 0.9rem 1.25rem;
  }

  li {
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }

  .effective-date {
    color: #6b7280;
  }
</style>
